does this thing do work  it is a monstrous cleanup type gun that  finishes kills at range  it can even be effective at mid-range  sometimes but obviously it shines the  brightest and close quarter encounters  now there are some inconsistencies with  the gun despite its popularity  folks online have complained that this  seems to be a gun where  other people who use it win but when i  use it i lose  still its damage is undeniable destroy  your enemies with one shot at close  range in the gut  the arm the leg wherever take your pick  [Music]  the m2 the m2 carl gustav  recoilless anti-tank rifle is in a  slightly different position than the  rest of the entries on this list and  that it is utilized situationally  with the intention of disabling vehicles  obviously  the m2 is a powerful addition to the  engineer's arsenal and although the  purpose of the weapon  is to operate as an anti-tank and  anti-air weapon at times players used  the m2 as an  anti-infantry weapon much to the ire of  other players  by design the m2 had huge areas of  impact  but contrary to other big anti-vehicle  weapons like an rpg  the m2 had less total damage but a lot  of splash damage  this meant that it might take a couple  direct hits to disable the tank  but you could wipe out infantry just by  shooting in the general vicinity  the main gripe that the online community  had with the m2  was that it just didn't quite fit the  goal of playing the engineer class  because being forgiving enough to let  the engineer moonlight as an assault  class  using their arsenal as an anti-infantry  kit just gave the engineers a larger  advantage over selecting other classes  which isn't fair and the extremely  forgiving splash damage led to a lot  of frustration this gun might feel like  it's not  quite as overpowered or blatantly broken  but no one can deny that it is extremely  above  average at its worst and infuriating to  go up against at its best  one of the most common guns in the game  for the assault class and extremely  popular  the aek 971 sports several advantages  for starters the majority of its stats  are all above average  allowing the weapon to be reliable in  all close encounter engagements  as well as some fights at medium range  for more skilled players that can handle  its recoil  the gun has a very high rate of fire and  feels good to use at  900 rpm making it the second fastest  rifle in the game  a lot of posts online are of the opinion  that the gun is very low skill to  utilize  since so many of its stats are forgiving  which to them  means that the weapon must be a crutch  whether or not this is true  is hard for me to say personally because  there is a consistent trend  where if more players are using a weapon  and shifting the meta  then the assumption becomes that all the  low-skilled players must be using the  weapon as well  which isn't necessarily true however it  is hard to deny the weapons popularity  and advantages granting the aek 971  a spot on this list alright  once again the smg's show their faces on  this list for being overpowered  this time with yet another battlefield 1  weapon the smg-0818  it's perks incredible magazine size and  fast time to kill  the only close quarter counter possible  is a model 10a hunter or another  comparable shotgun  now the smg-0818 does qualify as a  contender for the question of  is it truly broken or is it simply  annoying and a popular weapon of choice  for newbies  the sentiment online is that the  smg-0818 is the ultimate weapon of  choice for  bad players and is a low-skilled ceiling  weapon  new players can just spray and pray  letting the gun do all the heavy lifting  as a dlc weapon it takes a minute to  unlock  but it's not particularly difficult  meaning that the weapon was quickly in  the hands of hordes of players  wreaking havoc across the battlefield  battlefield hardline the underrated dark  horse of the franchise  the forgotten middle child although  battlefield veterans might overlook  hardline at times  one thing that absolutely refused to be  forgotten was the k10  smg similar to the nambu type 2a that  appeared in battlefield v  and made our part 1 list of most broken  weapons the k10 smg introduced  a lot of familiar traits specifically  one of the highest firing rates in the  franchise  with an rpm of 1200 that's not to say  the k10 didn't have any drawbacks  there is a significant damage drop off  to anything beyond 30 meters  but if you were in that sweet spot  between 10 to 30 meters  there was a high chance you were about  to become godlike the small magazine of  the k10 meant constantly reloading  however not only was the reload fast  enough to make this drawback minor  but the time to kill was so strong you  could wipe out multiple enemies before  the magazine had emptied  the nambu type 2a was certified busted  in the later game  in battlefield v but the k10 did it all  first  now here's a bonus one that will make  anyone grown in despair if you played  battlefield 4.  it's not a weapon but a utility the suav  aircraft was a super small moving drone  that could cause road kills meaning one  hit ko utility by simply flying  close enough to opponents which means  we're all just living  in one big meme simulation absolutely  hilarious if you were using it  absolutely painful to watch if you had  any self-respect or empathy  and nothing short of infuriating if you  died to it  so many of you gave me great weapons to  hunt down online and read up on how  broken they were pre-patched throughout  battlefield's history so a big  thank you personally out of all of them  i found the suav to be  genuinely appalling but from a pure  weapons point of view  i think the m26 dart took the crown  because it was  literally busted like you had to  activate an actual glitch  now i've always thought that dice  sandboxes were pretty balanced once the  patches and fixes came in  but i want to know what you guys think  so let me know if there's any guns that  i missed  and if there's enough you can count on  seeing me return with a part three  thanks for watching  you
 

